dropped the body
--
N5008 [expr.static.cast]/7 with [conv.array]: `static_cast<E *>(arr)' for
an array lvalue `arr' of type E[N] applies the array-to-pointer
conversion.  In a function template with a reference-to-array parameter
(`E (&arr)[N]', here spelled with type_identity_t as libstdc++ does) the
front end reports "type mismatch on static_cast" and drops the
constructor.  This is libstdc++'s span(type_identity_t<element_type>
(&)[N]) constructor (span:189), dropped in the <format> descs;
test_libstdcxx.desc constructs a std::span from an array and forbids
only that drop.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept both programs.
Pre-existing (fails on bin52).
